# Cloudflare Pages security headers. https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Two tiers. The active block below is behaviour-neutral: none of these
# directives govern how scripts/styles/images/connections load, so they cannot
# break the app. They deliver clickjacking protection and base-uri/object
# hardening today.
#
# The resource-directive CSP (script-src/style-src/connect-src/img-src/...) that
# would additionally backstop XSS is drafted at the bottom and left disabled: a
# too-tight script-src breaks Mantine's inline ColorSchemeScript and the React
# Router bootstrap, so it must be finalised against a real build and reviewed in
# the running app before enabling.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'

